// REJECTS: Field 'table' is required
//
// Inside `-> Relational #{ ... }#` the body is re-lexed with PersistenceRelationalLexer-
// Grammar, a separate 32-keyword grammar whose entry rule is
// `definition: (table | database | temporality)* EOF` -- three stars and an EOF. An EMPTY
// island is a complete parse; `table` and `database` are required by
// PersistenceRelationalParseTreeWalker and `temporality` genuinely is optional.
//
// The island is also where the same spellings mean different things: `database:` here is
// TARGET_RELATIONAL_DATABASE, not the SINK_DATABASE of the outer grammar, and `DateTime`
// and `None` are re-declared too. So this file is checking that the right grammar was
// reached, as much as that the field is required.
###Persistence
Persistence test::persistence::neg::RelationalTargetNoTable
{
  doc: 'a relational persistence target that names no table';
  trigger: Manual;
  service: test::persistence::Service;
  serviceOutputTargets:
  [
    TDS
    {
      keys:
      [
        foo
      ]
      datasetType: Delta
      {
        actionIndicator: None;
      }
    }
    ->
    Relational
    #{
      database: test::persistence::Database;
      temporality: None
      {
        auditing: None;
        updatesHandling: Overwrite;
      }
    }#
  ];
}
